<ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id="ceda5610-5e09-427f-8546-f3b2035442ff" ac:name="info" ac:schema-version="1">
  <ac:parameter ac:name="title">Context</ac:parameter>
  <ac:rich-text-body>
    <p>This page is for TwinCAT PLC developers already using the LCLS TwinCAT Motion Library v1 and would like to start using v2. The page provides additional information and best practices for using v2 of the motion library going forward. It covers what the library is for, the version to use, the dependencies that must be in place, and the configuration parameters you set before writing and deploying a PLC application code. Worked sample programs are provided separately to walk through each application pattern end-to-end</p>
  </ac:rich-text-body>
</ac:structured-macro>
<h2>Overview</h2>
<p>The motion library v2 provides a layered abstraction for Hutches' motion control only for Beckhoff/TwinCAT 4026 and onwards. It lets an application author wire up single-axis devices, multi-axis named-position "state movers" (parallel or sequential), and PMPS-integrated devices without re-implementing the underlying motion, persistence, and protection logic.</p>
<p>The library is organized in layers, from lowest to highest:</p>
<ul>
  <li data-uuid="0bd4b672-9a97-49cd-bc6b-2d61c42a3f2d">
    <strong>Drive layer</strong>: single-axis abstraction: hardware or simulated axes, persistent parameters, limits and interlocks, and the motion-request state machine. Motion parameters (velocity, acceleration, deceleration, jerk) are owned at this layer and persist across PLC restarts. The drive layer also ships optional integrations: EPS interlocks, gantry auto-coupling, and a backlash-compensation wrapper around <code>MC_BacklashCompensation</code>.</li>
  <li data-uuid="d489df0e-e31b-4b43-b5f8-772d28841b42">
    <strong>State-mover layer</strong>: moves N motors to named position states, either in parallel (<code>FB_PositionStateND</code>) or sequentially (<code>FB_PositionStateSequenceND</code>).</li>
  <li data-uuid="dea0b463-c038-4610-9d47-0be99a4a398c">
    <strong>PMPS layer</strong>: adds beam-parameter management and machine-protection enforcement on top of the state movers (<code>FB_PositionStatePMPSND, FB_PositionStateSequencePMPSND</code>).</li>
</ul>
<p>Each layer builds on the one below it. A simple device needs only the drive layer; a multi-position device adds the state-mover layer; a protection-aware device adds the PMPS layer.</p>
<h2>Library Version &amp; Platform Compatibility</h2>
<p>Use this version: <code>LCLS_Tc_Motion releases v2.1.0</code>
</p>
<p>Requirement:<code> TwinCAT XAE &amp; XAR &gt;= 4026</code>
</p>
